        "card_1": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "leaf",
            "numeral": "",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Natural materials",
            "tagline": "",
            "text": "<p>Baby alpaca, Cheviot wool, horsehair, vegetable horsehair, yak, mohair, cashmere, silk, linen, organic cotton and Orange Fiber. Fibres that were grown rather than extruded, and that can be carded, washed and laid again.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "link": "",
            "link_label": "",
            "open_panel": false
          }
        },
        "card_2": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "hand",
            "numeral": "",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Handmade production",
            "tagline": "",
            "text": "<p>Two artisans build each system start to finish, in Italy. No line, no tooling to amortise, no minimum run. A bed is made when it is ordered, which is why there is nothing to discount and nothing to clear.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "link": "",
            "link_label": "",
            "open_panel": false
          }
        },
        "card_3": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "wrench",
            "numeral": "",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "Repairability",
            "tagline": "",
            "text": "<p>Every layer is reachable. Fibres can be opened, redistributed and replaced; upholstery can be taken off and remade. A system is a set of serviceable parts, not a sealed unit.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "link": "",
            "link_label": "",
            "open_panel": false
          }
        },
        "card_4": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "recycle",
            "numeral": "",
            "eyebrow": "",
            "title": "15 + 15",
            "tagline": "",
            "text": "<p>At year fifteen the mattress returns to the artisans who made it and its comfort, integrity and life are restored for the fifteen years ahead. The alternative — replacement — is the thing this service exists to avoid.</p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "link": "",
            "link_label": "",
            "open_panel": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "card_1",
